build-script: make --cross-compile-hosts=linux-static-<arch> usable.

What: fix a wrong enum name (StdlibDeploymentTarget.Musl -> LinuxStatic), parse
host names that contain a dash ("linux-static-aarch64") with rsplit, and emit a
CMake toolchain file for the linux-static platform (sysroot = <musl-path>/<arch>,
target = <arch>-swift-linux-musl).
Why: build-script is still used for the native LLVM, cmark and for generating
the cross LLVM build directory. Not related to iSH.
Upstream: plain bug fixes for an untested code path; should be acceptable.

Apply inside the `swift` repository: git apply <this file>
---
diff --git a/utils/build-script b/utils/build-script
--- a/utils/build-script
+++ b/utils/build-script
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@
         return targets
     elif host_target.platform.name == 'linux':
         if args.build_linux_static:
-            targets.append(getattr(StdlibDeploymentTarget.Musl,
+            targets.append(getattr(StdlibDeploymentTarget.LinuxStatic,
                                    host_target.arch))
 
     return targets
